Sovereign AI】\nL112: \nL113: ### Best Practices\nL114: \nL115:   * 【58†Latency and Performance】\nL116:   * 【59†Prompt Caching】\nL117:   * 【60†Spend Controls】\nL118:   * 【61†Capping Shared Agent Keys】\nL119:   * 【62†Uptime Optimization】\nL120:   * 【63†Reasoning Tokens】\nL121: \nL122: ### Providers\nL123: \nL124:   * 【64†Integration】\nL125:   * 【65†Traffic Routing】\nL126: ### Community\nL127: \nL128:   * 【66†Frameworks and Integrations Overview】\nL129:   * 【67†Awesome OpenRouter】\nL130:   * 【68†Effect AI SDK】\nL131:   * 【69†Arize AX】\nL132:   * 【70†LangChain】\nL133:   * 【71†LiveKit】\nL134:   * 【72†Langfuse】\nL135:   * 【73†Mastra】\nL136:   * 【74†OpenAI SDK】\nL137:   * 【75†Anthropic Agent SDK】\nL138:   * 【76†PydanticAI】\nL139:   * 【77†Render】\nL140:   * 【78†Replit】\nL141:   * 【79†TanStack AI】\nL142:   * 【80†Jev (TypeSafe)】\nL143:   * 【81†Jev Tutorial】\nL144:   * 【82†Multimodal Decisions】\nL145:   * 【83†TypeSafe SDK (Jev)】\nL146:   * 【84†Vercel AI SDK】\nL147:   * 【85†Xcode】\nL148:   * 【86†Zapier】\nL149:   * 【87†Infisical】\nL150: \nL151: Multimodal\nL152: # Image Inputs\nL153: \nL154: How to send images to OpenRouter models\nL155: \nL156: Copy page Copy page\nL157: Requests with images, to multimodel models, are available via the `/api/v1/chat/completions` API with a multi-part `messages` parameter. The `image_url` can either be a URL or a base64-encoded image. Note that multiple images can be sent in separate content array entries. The number of images you can send in a single request varies per provider and per model. Due to how the content is parsed, we recommend sending the text prompt first, then the images.\nL158: If the images must come first, we recommend putting it in the system prompt. OpenRouter supports both direct URLs and base64-encoded data for images:\nL159:   * URLs: More efficient for publicly accessible images as they don’t require local encoding\nL160:   * Base64: Required for local files or private images that aren’t publicly accessible\nL161: ###\nL162: \nL163: 【88†​】\nL164: \nL165: Using Image URLs\nL166: \nL167: Here’s how to send an image using a URL:\nL168: \nL169: ###\nL170: \nL171: 【89†​】\nL172: \nL173: Using Base64 Encoded Images\nL174: \nL175: For locally stored images, you can send them using base64 encoding. Here’s how to do it: Supported image content types are:\nL176: \nL177:   * `image/png`\nL178:   * `image/jpeg`\nL179:   * `image/webp`\nL180:   * `image/gif`\nL181: \nL182: Was this page helpful?\nL183: \nL184: Yes No\nL185: \nL186: 【12†PDFs】【14†Video Understanding】\n"